    {
      "id": "claim_bdd21ee8a1284c84830f6e42969bf53c",
      "statement": "The Service enforces+blocks: the engine evaluates and passes its verdict via Request.PreDecision while the service persists, parks, and resolves; it is constructed with db, bus, log, and the process-constant dataDir; EvaluateRules evaluates builtins (BuiltinsFor) + the turn's config rules (no session always-rules), and DecisionFor re-evaluates builtins + config + the session's persisted always-rules (db.AlwaysRules; load failure degrades to no always-rules) with the catch-all '*' allow standing in for the no-rule default only for known core actions (corePermissions) so unknown actions fall through to ask.",
